  "interpretation": "Current renderer matrix/draw CPU work competes with cold model parsing. Metadata caching already removes measured duplicate FST/texmeta/JSON requests. Parsed-template and bitmap ownership optimizations need independent actual proof.",
  "limitations": [
    "Intervals are polling bounds, not exact full-image/material readiness.",
    "FBX parsing is synchronous main-thread work; worker decode and fbxPrepareWait/compressedColor/shaderPrepare are sums across overlapping asynchronous operations.",
    "graphicsSubmit includes renders before connection and throughout loading; whole-phase sums cannot be divided by the after-connection interval as pure loading CPU time.",
    "HTTP admission totals include requests after the first modelJobsIdle sample; initial network critical path cannot be reconstructed from censored aggregate entries or the 250-entry Resource Timing buffer.",
    "Known bytes omit failed/unknown responses; byte totals do not establish link saturation.",
    "Both reports retain unsupported/failing model/image requests; reaching modelJobsIdle is not all-content support or fluid movement acceptance.",
    "Current and prior runs differ in instrumentation/source; their one-pair loading difference is not an optimization gain.",
    "No endurance tests or hardware microphone claims."
  ]
